[% /* Generates the readme artifact. */ %]# [%= emitCtx.get("projectName") %]

Generated AWS serverless project from the PSM model. Implement the service-owned application use cases under `services/<service>/internal/application` before exercising modeled business flows.

## Generated Commands

- `make validate` validates generated model reports, contracts, and SAM template.
- `make build` builds generated source.
- `make test` runs generated tests.
- `make deploy STAGE=[%= emitCtx.get("defaultStageName") %]` deploys with `infrastructure/samconfig.toml`.
- `source scripts/emulator-env.sh` selects the local Floci/LocalStack endpoint for CLI and SDK tests.

## Local AWS emulator

The generated project is compatible with the MODRISS Floci emulator by default. Start the emulator
from the repository root (`scripts/aws-emulator.ps1 start` or `./scripts/aws-emulator.sh start`),
then source `scripts/emulator-env.sh` before `make test` or local SAM commands. Set
`AWS_EMULATOR=localstack` for a LocalStack compatibility run.

## Project Layout

- `services/<service>/cmd/<function>` contains each service-owned Lambda entry point.
- `services/<service>/contracts`, `workflows`, and `tests` keep interfaces and verification beside their owning service.
- `services/<service>/internal` contains service-owned domain, application, and adapter scaffolds. The generator creates the notes and Lambda use-case stubs once, then leaves those files to developers.
- `platform/runtime` contains generated cross-cutting runtime support and low-level AWS SDK helpers. Service-specific domain and adapter code belongs under the owning service's `internal` tree.
- `contracts/public/schemas` contains system-wide generated schema catalogs.
- `infrastructure/units/<deployment-unit>/template.yaml` contains each generated SAM/CloudFormation template.
- `infrastructure/environments` contains stage configuration; `infrastructure/samconfig.toml` contains SAM CLI defaults.
- `docs` contains generated architecture, operations, deployment, security, and runbook documentation.
- `generated` contains traceability and generation reports.

[% if (AWSPSMSTORAGE!RdsDbCluster.all.notEmpty()) { %]
## Relational storage

`database/*.sql` describes the initial PostgreSQL schema; `database/manifest.json` is its deployment
contract. Aurora clusters, Serverless v2 writers, and generated credential secrets are modeled in
the templates. `scripts/deploy.sh` initializes the schema after stack deployment using Python/boto3.
MODRISS Test deployment performs the same initialization and records its real Data API calls.
An unchanged schema keeps existing data. Changed schemas stop for a reviewed migration; no tables
are silently dropped or altered. SQL relationships/foreign keys require explicit design rather
than being inferred from similarly named fields.

Generated functions receive `<STORE_PREFIX>_RESOURCE_ARN`, `<STORE_PREFIX>_SECRET_ARN`, and
`<STORE_PREFIX>_DATABASE`. `runtime.NewRelationalStore(ctx, "<STORE_PREFIX>")` loads these values;
its `Execute` method accepts SDK `SqlParameter` values and an optional transaction ID. Use
`WithTransaction` for operations that must commit together. Business handlers still need their
business logic. Credentials are generated outside source; review application database users/grants
before production. The helper honors `AWS_ENDPOINT_URL` for local Floci evaluation.
[% } %]

